From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:52:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Power the NVIDIA GPU off at boot under
 macOS

macOS has no driver for the Kepler GPU of the W541 (none since Big Sur,
OpenCore Legacy Patcher root patches aside), and with the GPU enabled
in the setup nothing takes it over: it stays in D0, powered and idle at
the clocks it comes up with. OpenCore configurations turn it off with
an SSDT that calls the _OFF of the OEM firmware, a path this DSDT does
not have, or hide it from the drivers (-wegnoegpu), which leaves it
powered.

Under macOS (ISDW), call the _OFF of the power resource of the PEG port
from the _INI of the port: link down, PERST#, rails off, the sequence
of the runtime power management of Linux. _INI runs only with the port
present, the GPU enabled in the setup; a wake from S3 keeps the GPU off
(mb_late_romstage_setup()). Linux and Windows are left alone.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init. In
acpiexec on its DSDT, with _OSI ("Darwin") answered, the _INI of PEGP
sets the link disable bit of the port and clears the power and PERST#
bits of PMH7 register 0x50 (0x88 and 0x08 to 0x00); without "Darwin"
it changes nothing. The other ACPI checks give the same results.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/dgpu.asl | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/dgpu.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/dgpu.asl
index fe913b3a4a..aa7b5aa8ce 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/dgpu.asl
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/dgpu.asl
@@ -215,6 +215,20 @@ Scope (\_SB.PCI0.PEGP)
 
 	/* D3cold is supported while in S0 */
 	Name (_S0W, 4)
+
+	/*
+	 * Under macOS, off from the start. It has no driver for this Kepler GPU
+	 * (none since Big Sur), and a GPU that no driver takes over stays in D0,
+	 * powered, at the clocks it comes up with. The same _OFF as the runtime
+	 * power management of Linux reaches: link down, PERST#, rails off. A
+	 * wake from S3 keeps the GPU off (mb_late_romstage_setup()).
+	 */
+	Method (_INI, 0, Serialized)
+	{
+		If (\ISDW ()) {
+			\_SB.PCI0.PEGP.PGPR._OFF ()
+		}
+	}
 }
 
 Scope (\_SB.PCI0.PEGP.DEV0)
